ni":"فَإِنْ حَآجُّوكَ فَقُلْ أَسْلَمْتُ وَجْهِىَ لِلَّهِ وَمَنِ ٱتَّبَعَنِ ۗ وَقُل لِّلَّذِينَ أُوتُوا۟ ٱلْكِتَـٰبَ وَٱلْأُمِّيِّـۧنَ ءَأَسْلَمْتُمْ ۚ فَإِنْ أَسْلَمُوا۟ فَقَدِ ٱهْتَدَوا۟ ۖ وَّإِن تَوَلَّوْا۟ فَإِنَّمَا عَلَيْكَ ٱلْبَلَـٰغُ ۗ وَٱللَّهُ بَصِيرٌۢ بِٱلْعِبَادِ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"if they argue with you [Prophet], say, ‘I have devoted myself to God alone and so have my followers.’ Ask those who were given the Scripture, as well as those without one, ‘Do you too devote yourselves to Him alone?’ If they do, they will be guided, but if they turn away, your only duty is to convey the message. God is aware of His servants.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"فَإِنْ","en_gloss":"Then if","transliteration":"fa-in","verse_key":"3:20"},{"pos":2,"ar":"حَآجُّوكَ","en_gloss":"they argue with you","transliteration":"ḥājjūka","verse_key":"3:20"},{"pos":3,"ar":"فَقُلْ","en_gloss":"then say","transliteration":"faqul","verse_key":"3:20"},{"pos":4,"ar":"أَسْلَمْتُ","en_gloss":"I have submitted","transliteration":"aslamtu","verse_key":"3:20"},{"pos":5,"ar":"وَجْهِىَ","en_gloss":"myself","transliteration":"wajhiya","verse_key":"3:20"},{"pos":6,"ar":"لِلَّهِ","en_gloss":"to Allah","transliteration":"lillahi","verse_key":"3:20"},{"pos":7,"ar":"وَمَنِ","en_gloss":"and (those) who","transliteration":"wamani","verse_key":"3:20"},{"pos":8,"ar":"ٱتَّبَعَنِ ۗ","en_gloss":"follow me","transliteration":"ittabaʿani","verse_key":"3:20"},{"pos":9,"ar":"وَقُل","en_gloss":"And say","transliteration":"waqul","verse_key":"3:20"},{"pos":10,"ar":"لِّلَّذِينَ","en_gloss":"to those who","transliteration":"lilladhīna","verse_key":"3:20"},{"pos":11,"ar":"أُوتُوا۟","en_gloss":"were given","transliteration":"ūtū","verse_key":"3:20"},{"pos":12,"ar":"ٱلْكِتَـٰبَ","en_gloss":"the Book","transliteration":"l-kitāba","verse_key":"3:20"},{"pos":13,"ar":"وَٱلْأُمِّيِّـۧنَ","en_gloss":"and the unlettered people","transliteration":"wal-umiyīna","verse_key":"3:20"},{"pos":14,"ar":"ءَأَسْلَمْتُمْ ۚ","en_glos